WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:04.360
Of the six Infinity Stones, the Soul Stone
is arguably the trickiest to wrap your head

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:05.360
around.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:09.320
Of particular concern is the question of what
happens to the stone if it's returned to the

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:10.849
place from which it was taken.

00:00:10.849 --> 00:00:15.559
Thankfully, the writers of Avengers: Endgame
have come forward to explain exactly what

00:00:15.559 --> 00:00:17.140
happened to the Soul Stone in the film.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:18.760
First, a little refresher.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:24.140
Avengers: Endgame sees Black Widow and Hawkeye
take a trip to the mysterious planet of Vormir

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:28.040
on a mission to pluck the Soul Stone out of
time before Thanos or his minions can acquire

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:29.040
it.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:34.040
Hawkeye ultimately obtains the Stone after
Black Widow heroically throws herself off

00:00:34.059 --> 00:00:38.809
the planet's massive cliff, echoing the same
sequence from Infinity War in which Thanos

00:00:38.809 --> 00:00:40.740
killed Gamora for the stone.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:44.980
Before he retires to a life of slow dancing
with Peggy Carter at the end of the movie,

00:00:44.989 --> 00:00:49.629
Captain America travels back to the past to
place the Stone in the same spot it was in

00:00:49.629 --> 00:00:51.269
before Black Widow sacrificed herself.

00:00:51.269 --> 00:00:56.379
As MCU fans now know, there are pretty specific
rules for what has to happen before someone

00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:58.280
can take the Soul Stone from Vormir.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:03.659
"In order to take the stone, you must lose
that which you love.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:06.080
A soul...for a soul."

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:11.420
After Infinity War and Endgame, we've seen
that part of the process go down twice.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:15.520
But we've never before seen anyone try to
put that Soul Stone back.

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:18.369
How did Cap successfully return the Soul Stone?

00:01:18.369 --> 00:01:22.830
And, perhaps more importantly, would putting
the Soul Stone back revive the person who

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:23.850
died for it?

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:28.850
Christopher Markus and Stephen McFeely explained
during a recent episode of CinemaBlend's HeroBlend

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:34.890
podcast that Captain America faced no trouble
returning the Soul Stone, but sadly, the soul-for-a-soul

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:39.480
exchange that Black Widow and Hawkeye made
with the keeper of the Stone, Red Skull, wasn't

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:40.740
reversed in that moment.

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:42.760
"How does one return the Soul Stone?"

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:43.780
"It's a good question.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:46.080
I think it is an everlasting exchange."

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:47.090
"There's a slot."

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:48.400
"That's right.

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:52.180
That's right, it's like an old-time bank."

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:57.200
Unfortunately, this shows that just because
the Soul Stone was returned doesn't mean that

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:00.440
those who were sacrificed to retrieve it get
to come back to life.

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:04.740
The exchange is permanent, and the soul that
was sacrificed can't be retrieved.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:05.880
As Markus put it,

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:14.500
While fans held onto the hope that Black Widow
could perhaps be resurrected once Captain

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:18.501
America put the Soul Stone back on Vormir,
that's apparently not going to happen, as

00:02:18.501 --> 00:02:21.020
it's simply not the way the Soul Stone works.

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:25.080
Cap returning the Soul Stone only patched
up the timeline, it didn't undo Black Widow's

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:26.080
death.

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:30.740
This has a huge repercussion on the future
of the Marvel Cinematic Universe, since Marvel

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:34.159
Studios is currently developing a Black Widow
solo movie.

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:37.760
How that's going to work with a dead Black
Widow is sort of up in the air.

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:41.780
It's possible the movie will be a prequel,
giving us the backstory for Black Widow that

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:44.500
the other MCU movies have only ever teased
at.

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:49.600
It's also possible that she really is alive
out there somewhere, brought back by Hulk's

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:53.360
use of the Infinity Stones without him or
anyone else knowing about it.

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:58.360
It's also possible that the movie will focus
on an entirely different Black Widow; at this

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:00.060
point, we just don't know.

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:04.320
While Marvel has kept quiet about the film,
there have been some clues as to when Black

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:06.140
Widow's solo adventure might be set.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:10.500
Past reports pin the film as being a period
piece, set partially in Natasha Romanoff's

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:14.620
younger years working with the KGB, and then
jumping forward to 15 years after the fall

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:15.880
of the KGB.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:20.600
If Markus and McFeely are to be believed,
and there truly is no way that Nat can be

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:24.909
resurrected, then there isn't any other point
in time that Black Widow screenwriter Jac

00:03:24.909 --> 00:03:29.840
Schaeffer can place the film other than years
before the events of Avengers: Endgame.

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:33.740
Losing Black Widow in Avengers: Endgame was
a painful experience.

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:37.050
And though she may never come back to life
in the present day to join the Avengers who

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:41.660
lived through the film, it looks like super-spy
is all set to make at least one more appearance

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:44.060
on the big screen before fans say goodbye.

